  "status_text": "Thirty-two settings can expose a circuit failure that every group of thirty-one misses. Lean checked the exact cutoff for three watched lights and at most two bit-flipping gates, with free constants and no limit on how many AND or OR gates can be used. Each gate reads at most two wires. Switches come on in order, and each setting allows a list of light patterns. Any failure shows up on at most 32 original settings, and a checked example needs all 32. With at least one watched light, each extra light or bit-flipping gate allowed doubles the worst-case cutoff (L-lib-1357).",
